WEBVTT

NOTE Free version demo — issue-worm free shell
NOTE Transcript: docs/assets/demo-transcripts.md#free-version-demo

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
This is issue-worm, the free shell.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:11.000
I've got a GitHub issue here that's already scoped — it has an
Implementation notes section with FILES: and DONE: lines,

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
so the deterministic pre-check will let it through.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.000
I run issue-worm build against the issue and the repo.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
First it checks the issue is scoped enough to dispatch.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Then it hands the issue to the coder — a local Ollama model by default —

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.000
which writes the proposed changes straight into the working tree.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.000
That's the whole run: one pass, no verifier, no retry loop.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.000
The coder has produced a diff, and it's up to me to review it,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.000
run the tests, and open the PR myself.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:02.000
That's the honest trade-off of the free tier: it's genuinely useful
for a well-scoped task,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.000
but you're still in the loop for everything after the code is written.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:15.000
If you want AI to run the whole pipeline — triage, coding, judging its
own failures, and drafting the PR —

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.000
that's issue-worm-pro.
